                <pb facs="0571" n="483" sameAs="frus:frus1933v05/pg483"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.01/32: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gibson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-10-13T15:00:00-03:00">October 13, 1933—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>91. Minister for Foreign Affairs would value any information as to our progress
                    toward recognition of Cuban government. Says he <pb facs="0572" n="484"
                        xml:id="pg484"/> is anxious to follow our lead in this matter of primary
                    interest to us but is now at a disadvantage in standing off pressure for
                    recognition through lack of up-to-date information. Suggest Department keep me
                    advised of developments from time to time.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gibson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
